From 61c795e2af70ba668f470959d4fb7b95849fa591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axis Dev <axis-dev@example.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:44:58 +0000
Subject: feat: replace RevenueCat with Paddle for subscription billing

Swaps RevenueCat out entirely in favor of Paddle across web checkout and
entitlement checks.

- lib/paddle-plans.ts: maps Axis plan IDs (starter/pro/advanced) to Paddle
  price IDs via env vars
- lib/paddle.ts: Paddle.js wrapper (init + openCheckout), replacing
  lib/revenuecat.ts
- app/api/paddle/webhook/route.ts: new webhook endpoint syncing Paddle
  subscription.* events into Supabase. Paddle's client SDK has no
  CustomerInfo-style entitlement object like RevenueCat's, so this is now
  the source of truth for subscription state instead of a client call.
- supabase/migrations/20260827000001_paddle_subscriptions.sql: new
  subscriptions table + has_axis_pro_v1() RPC, RLS-protected, written only
  via the webhook's service role client
- hooks/useAxisPro.ts: reads entitlement from Supabase instead of
  RevenueCat's CustomerInfo; same public hook shape so call sites elsewhere
  are unaffected
- components/Paywall.tsx: rebuilt as an Axis-owned plan/interval picker
  that opens Paddle's overlay checkout, since Paddle has no equivalent to
  RevenueCat's embeddable presentPaywall
- hooks/use-auth.tsx: dropped Purchases.configure() on sign-in; Paddle
  instead receives the Supabase user ID as checkout custom_data, which the
  webhook uses to link the resulting subscription back to the account
- next.config.ts: swapped RevenueCat CSP origins for Paddle's
  (buy.paddle.com, checkout-service.paddle.com, cdn.paddle.com)
- package.json: -@revenuecat/purchases-js, +@paddle/paddle-js
  +@paddle/paddle-node-sdk
- .env.example: new Paddle env vars, pre-filled with the live price IDs
  created for Starter/Pro/Advanced (monthly + annual)

Verified: npm install, tsc --noEmit, eslint, and next build all pass clean.
